ifically the AA pair).\n\nReason: The Landlord is close to winning (4 cards left), so I must block his low single (5) with a high card to force out his top cards. Playing the single Queen is the most efficient move because it is high enough to force a response from the Landlord (forcing a K, A, or 2) while allowing me to keep my pair of Aces intact for future defense or control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦Q"]}'}
